        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/densh-header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>What do <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/jet-set-radio\">Jet Set Radio</a>, the PS1-era Tony Hawk's games, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/hi-fi-rush\">Hi-Fi Rush</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/olliolli\">OlliOlli</a> all have in common? Well, aside from being clear influences on Denshattack!, they are all cult classics: games that remain relevant, popular, and influential way beyond their respective eras. And it looks like they've got another stablemate in Undercoders' unlikely arcade grind-'em-up. Because this game is incredible.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/denshattack-review\">Read more</a></p>",
